  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling Visceral Leishmaniasis (VL) in Asia &amp; Africa Lot 1 and Lot 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To tackle Visceral Leishmaniasis (VL) also known as Kala &#x2013;Azar, in South Asia and East Africa, this disease is spread by sandflies and when untreated leads to death in 95% of cases.  The programme will increase access to effective prevention and prompt treatment for VL and will  accelerate progress towards the elimination of VL in South Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
